      </Table>
      <h2 id="oadp-cli-admin-bsl_oadp-cli-plugin" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backup storage location management commands<a href="#oadp-cli-admin-bsl_oadp-cli-plugin" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can use the OADP command-line interface (CLI) to create, view, set, and delete backup storage locations (BSLs). Backup storage locations define where backup data is stored, such as an object storage bucket.</p>
      <h3 id="oadp-cli-admin-bsl-prereqs_oadp-cli-plugin" class="group scroll-mt-20">Prerequisites<a href="#oadp-cli-admin-bsl-prereqs_oadp-cli-plugin" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <ul>
      <li>The OADP CLI plugin is installed and configured in admin mode.</li>
      <li>You are logged in to the OpenShift Container Platform cluster as a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 id="oadp-cli-admin-bsl-create_oadp-cli-plugin" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backup storage location creation command<a href="#oadp-cli-admin-bsl-create_oadp-cli-plugin" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>To create a backup storage location, use the following command:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp backup-location create <bsl_name> [flags]"} lang="terminal" />
      <p><strong>Flags for the </strong><code>oc oadp backup-location create</code><strong> command</strong></p>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Flag</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Description</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--provider</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The name of the cloud provider, for example, <code>aws</code>, <code>gcp</code>, or <code>azure</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--bucket</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The name of the object storage bucket.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--prefix</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The path prefix within the bucket.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--credential</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The secret and key for the provider credentials in the format <code>SECRET_NAME=KEY</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--config</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The provider-specific configuration as <code>key=value</code> pairs.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--backup-sync-period</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The frequency at which to synchronize the backup contents from object storage.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>--request-timeout</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The timeout for the request to the Kubernetes API server.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp backup-location create my-bsl \\\n    --provider aws \\\n    --bucket my-velero-bucket \\\n    --prefix velero \\\n    --credential cloud-credentials=cloud"} lang="terminal" title="Example of the backup storage location creation command" />
      <h3 id="oadp-cli-admin-bsl-list_oadp-cli-plugin" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backup storage location listing command<a href="#oadp-cli-admin-bsl-list_oadp-cli-plugin" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>To list all backup storage locations, use the following command:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp backup-location get [<bsl_name>] [flags]"} lang="terminal" />
